---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CCUSAGE_DIFFERENCES } from '../lib/compare';

// Sourced from AGENTS.md ("Ground truth is the raw JSONL", the ccusage table,
// correctness rules 1-7), README.md, docs/design.md (cost modes),
// PacerCore/Pricing/CuratedPriceHistory.swift and docs/release-notes.
// The table is shared with /compare/ccusage/ (src/lib/compare.ts).
const differences = CCUSAGE_DIFFERENCES;
---

<Base
  title="How Pacer counts Claude Code usage | Pacer"
  description="Where Pacer's token, cost and rate-limit numbers come from, the rules it follows reading Claude Code's transcripts, and why its numbers differ from ccusage on purpose."
>
  <header class="wrap page-head">
    <h1>How Pacer counts</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Pacer's numbers come from the transcripts Claude Code writes on your Mac and from Anthropic's own rate-limit
      readings. This is how it reads them, and where it differs from ccusage on purpose.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="wrap prose">
    <section aria-labelledby="sources">
      <h2 id="sources">Where the numbers come from</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Tokens and cost</strong> come from Claude Code's transcripts: one line per request, in
          <code>~/.claude</code> and <code>~/.config/claude</code> (Pacer reads both when both exist), or in
          <code>CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR</code> when you set it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Rate limits</strong> come from Anthropic, asked with your Claude Code login every few minutes. Between
          readings Pacer estimates from what you've spent since the last one, and marks the estimate with a decimal.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Every request is kept.</strong> Totals can always be rebuilt from those raw records, so a fix to how
          Pacer counts corrects your history, not just what comes next.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="rules">
      <h2 id="rules">Rules it follows</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Each request counts once.</strong> A resumed session copies earlier turns into a new file. Pacer matches
          requests by their message and request IDs and counts each one once, whichever file it reads first.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Claude Code's internal placeholder entries are skipped.</strong> They are not requests anyone pays
          for.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A broken line never stops a scan.</strong> The last line of a session that is still being written is
          often cut off. Pacer skips a line it can't read rather than stopping.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Pacer checks itself daily.</strong> Once a day it compares every request Claude Code answered with its
          own records. Some calls never reach a transcript, such as "while you were away" recaps and conversation
          compactions, and the check allows for those.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="ccusage">
      <h2 id="ccusage">Why it differs from ccusage</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="https://github.com/ccusage/ccusage">ccusage</a> is a good command-line tool, and Pacer started as a
        port of it. Pacer's numbers are checked against the raw transcripts, not against ccusage, and where the two
        disagree it is usually one of these:
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap table-wrap">
    <table class="diff">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col"></th>
          <th scope="col">ccusage</th>
          <th scope="col">Pacer</th>
          <th scope="col">Why</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          differences.map((d) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{d.what}</th>
              <td data-label="ccusage">{d.ccusage}</td>
              <td data-label="Pacer">{d.pacer}</td>
              <td data-label="Why">{d.why}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap prose">
    <p>
      Where a comparison with ccusage disagrees on one of these, Pacer's number is the intended one. More on the two, and on
      the other trackers: <a href="/compare/">how Pacer compares</a>.
    </p>

    <section aria-labelledby="pricing">
      <h2 id="pricing">Pricing</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Two ways to count cost.</strong> Use the cost Claude Code reports, or have Pacer price every request
          from its tokens. Switch in Settings.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Rates</strong> come from public price catalogs, merged once and dated on our side so every Mac prices a
          change from the same moment, plus a reviewed price history for what catalogs can't hold: introductory rates,
          launch-day prices, changes over time. Each entry names its source. Both are public:
          <a href="/price-history.json">price-history.json</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A new model</strong> is priced as soon as a catalog lists it, and Pacer rebuilds the history it had
          before then.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <p class="small muted">
      The rules in full, with the tests that hold Pacer to them, are in the repo's
      <a href="https://github.com/EricAndrechek/Pacer/blob/main/AGENTS.md" data-track="docs">AGENTS.md</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .table-wrap {
    margin-block: 0.5rem 2rem;
  }
  .diff th[scope='row'] {
    font-weight: 700;
    white-space: nowrap;
    padding-right: 1.5rem;
  }
  .diff td:last-child {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    min-width: 28ch;
  }
  .diff td:nth-child(3) {
    font-weight: 550;
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .diff thead {
      position: absolute;
      width: 1px;
      height: 1px;
      overflow: hidden;
      clip: rect(0 0 0 0);
    }
    .diff,
    .diff tbody,
    .diff tr,
    .diff th,
    .diff td {
      display: block;
      width: 100%;
    }
    .diff tr {
      padding: 1rem 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    .diff th[scope='row'] {
      border: 0;
      padding: 0 0 0.35rem;
      font-size: 1.08rem;
    }
    .diff td {
      border: 0;
      padding: 0.15rem 0;
      min-width: 0;
    }
    .diff td::before {
      content: attr(data-label) ': ';
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--ink);
    }
  }
</style>
